+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-peak-pricing
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+Composer hint plugin for the Web UI. It occupies `conversation.input.right`, which is rendered in the visual gap between the permission control and model selector. The hint reads `现在是梁文峰时间` during Beijing peak hours and `现在是梁文谷时间` during idle hours; clicking it toggles a compact price card centered above the hint, and clicking elsewhere closes it.
+
+The Host fetches the [official DeepSeek pricing page](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/zh-cn/quick_start/pricing/), parses the model/version and idle/peak RMB prices, and serves a same-origin cached JSON response. The browser never performs a cross-origin request, so the feature does not depend on third-party CORS headers.
+
+## Model Experience
+
+The hint is presentation-only and adds no prompt text, session event, tool, or model-visible state. It only helps users understand the current official DeepSeek token pricing before sending a request.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+The card distinguishes cache-hit input, cache-miss input, and output prices. It does not change cache behavior or request routing.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- Prices are refreshed by the Host route every 15 minutes and the official source may change its table layout; parsing failures are shown as an actionable link to the source page.
+- The current idle/peak label uses Beijing time, matching the official pricing schedule. Idle prices are validated as exactly half of peak prices.
