+`HoverCard` keeps its portaled preview reachable across the anchor gap with a pointer-leave grace. Its floating surface reuses the same theme-aware material as `Menu`, so the background, border, shadow, and content colors follow the Web UI's light/dark setting. The default `trigger="hover"` opens after the dwell delay; `trigger="click"` toggles from the anchor, closes on an outside pointerdown or Escape, and leaves the card open while its content is read. `placement="right"` is the default, while `placement="top"` centers the card above the anchor and falls below only when the viewport has no room above. A consumer may also pass `copyText`: the card then exposes button semantics for pointer and keyboard activation, includes that value after the `copyLabel` prefix in its accessible name, writes the exact value through the package clipboard helper, and temporarily replaces its content with `copiedLabel` only after the host accepts the write. A non-collapsed text selection intersecting the card suppresses pointer-click activation, while success feedback retains the original card height and clears when the card closes or after one second. `copyLabel` and `copiedLabel` are label props because this zero-cordis atom cannot read the application locale; omitting `copyText` preserves the read/select-only card. Historical rationale: [the archived hover-card copy note](../../../.agents/notes/archived/feature/2026-07-31-hover-card-click-copy.md).
 
